from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
pages=[]
def page(title,body):
 pages.append(f'<section class="sheet"><div class="eyebrow">NEXT LEVEL · ITERATION 2 · 13 OCTOBER 2026</div><h1>{title}</h1>{body}<footer>Local synthetic exploration · no validated family score<span>{len(pages)+1:02}</span></footer></section>')
def fig(src,caption,kind='screen'):
 return f'<figure class="{kind}"><img src="{src}" alt="{caption}"><figcaption>{caption}</figcaption></figure>'
page('Understand them.<br><em>Choose how you show up.</em>','''<p class="lead">Test a parent practice loop with one feasible adjustment. Keep child understanding as context, not a fixed type or a grade.</p><div class="callout">Describe a moment, separate observation from interpretation, consider alternatives, choose an adult response, rehearse privately, try safely, then reflect.</div>'''+fig('diagrams/parent-practice-loop.svg','Proposed loop, not a therapy protocol or alliance measure.','diagram')+'''<h2>What changed</h2><p>The parent’s timing, wording, expectations, environment, listening and repair are the adjustable parts. Their capacity matters. The child can disagree, remain upset or choose space without failing the exercise.</p><p>Parent agency is a useful lever, not sole causation. Work, sleep, disability, poverty, health, school conditions and support affect what is possible. Sometimes the right next step is no new exercise and practical help.</p><p class="small">Iteration 1 remains preserved. Current recommendation is an experiment, not a relaunch. No real child records, model calls, recording or clinical measurement are part of this prototype.</p>''')
page('A different question<br><em>in the same hard moment.</em>','''<div class="two"><article><h2>Before</h2><p>“How can I make my child stop resisting?”</p></article><article><h2>After</h2><p>“What might I be missing, and what can I change while keeping a necessary boundary?”</p></article></div>'''+fig('screenshots/01-parent-adaptation-desktop.png','Synthetic morning episode: observation, parent interpretation and optional next step.')+'''<p>Review what actually happened. Their perspective is unknown. Offer possibilities rather than emotional mind-reading. Ask about capacity optionally; skip or choose a smaller plan.</p><p>A boundary is not justified merely because an adult set it. Consider what genuinely needs to stay safe/predictable and whether the rule, timing or delivery needs revision.</p><p class="small">Three original fixtures: school morning, cardboard-world joy and repair after raising one’s voice. The positive example helps the parent join without evaluating or taking over.</p>''')
page('An alliance analogy.<br><em>No alliance out of 100.</em>','''<table><tr><th>Construct</th><th>Do not substitute</th></tr><tr><td>Therapy working alliance</td><td>Bond, therapy goals/tasks do not equal the lifelong family relationship.</td></tr><tr><td>Parenting alliance (PAM)</td><td>Co-parent cooperation is not parent-child alliance.</td></tr><tr><td>Reflective functioning</td><td>Curiosity and uncertainty are not accurate mind-reading.</td></tr><tr><td>Autonomy support</td><td>Listening and genuine choice can coexist with structure.</td></tr><tr><td>Attachment security</td><td>Not current mood, compliance or a chat-inferred attachment type.</td></tr></table><p>The targeted review found no substantiated universal cross-age consumer-app composite with this intended interpretation. This is a bounded finding, not a prohibition on research or proof no related measure exists.</p><h2>Measures are not portable item banks</h2><p>CPRS measures parent-perceived closeness/conflict separately (owner: ages 3–12). PRFQ variants have age/informant limits and research-only guidance. P-PASS/POPS, IPPA, PACHIQ-R and PICCOLO need exact version, population, rights and change evidence. Rothbart’s group warns against individual assessment and universal norms.</p><p>A future instrument needs construct definition, qualitative work, rights checks, cognitive interviews, independent validation/invariance, change precision and evidence that displaying it helps more than no-score reflection. High alpha, satisfaction correlation or a 0–100 transformation is insufficient.</p><p class="small">Source: <a href="research/parent_iteration2_alliance_evidence.md">full measures review</a>; <a href="https://wai.profhorvath.com/what-is">WAI construct</a>; <a href="https://www.parinc.com/products/PAM">PAM owner</a>; <a href="https://www.ucl.ac.uk/brain-sciences/pals/psychoanalysis/research/parental-reflective-functioning-questionnaire-prfq">PRFQ guidance</a>. No proprietary items reproduced.</p>''')
page('Several perspectives.<br><em>No total grade.</em>',fig('screenshots/02-no-score-reflection-desktop.png','Attributed synthetic reflection; the child declined feedback. No inference about trust.','hero')+'''<p>Keep observation, adult interpretation, alternatives, child perspective, parent capacity and chosen action separate. Unknown stays unknown. A repair attempt does not establish completed repair.</p><p>“I tried it and they were still upset” is compatible with a useful parent change. Quietness may reflect fear or withdrawal; compliance is not enough to claim connection.</p><p class="small">Fixed parent-private fields, child quotes and hypotheses stay out of the initial brief. Corrected free text cannot be exported in this scripted demo; no semantic sensitivity classifier is implemented.</p>''')
page('A coherent direction.<br><em>An occupied category.</em>','''<table><tr><th>Comparator</th><th>Advertised overlap</th><th>What remains unverified</th></tr><tr><td>Mango Parent</td><td>Parent development, triggers/upbringing, Parent Replay, reset/repair, goals and reflective scores.</td><td>Execution and controlled outcomes; “reflective” does not mean validated.</td></tr><tr><td>Good Inside / GiGi</td><td>Regulation, understanding, connected boundaries, repair, co-parent sessions and reminders.</td><td>Full product-specific efficacy; public review located no controlled app study, not proof none exists.</td></tr><tr><td>Hatley</td><td>Longitudinal family context, strategy outcomes and cross-assistant access.</td><td>Comparative value, correction fidelity and claimed effectiveness.</td></tr><tr><td>Generic assistant</td><td>Same reviewed facts and parent context in a capable ongoing project.</td><td>Whether this guided workflow reduces effort or improves adult decisions.</td></tr></table><p>Good Inside is an acknowledged public reference, not an affiliation, copied branded method or validation shortcut. Its approach already supports parent adaptation; do not claim a missing feature from silence in marketing.</p><p>Program precedents have qualified evidence: COS-P trial had no main child-attachment/behavior effect; CPS tested a defined clinical population; Tuning in to Kids’ online trial included facilitator calls. None validates our autonomous adaptation.</p><p class="small"><a href="https://parentosapp.com/">Mango</a> · <a href="https://www.goodinside.com/workshops/">Good Inside workshops</a> · <a href="https://hatley.ai/">Hatley</a> · <a href="research/parent_iteration2_competitors.md">complete competitor/program review</a> · <a href="research/parent_iteration2_good_inside.md">Kennedy review and original exercise proposals</a>.</p>''')
page('Practice without pressure.<br><em>Share a small window.</em>',fig('screenshots/03-private-context-boundary-desktop.png','Exact synthetic export preview; no connector or transmission.')+'''<h2>Repair belongs to the adult</h2><p>Own the adult action and allow time, disagreement or space. Do not require forgiveness, a hug or reassurance. Repeated frightening conduct, abuse or danger needs appropriate human support, not another practice exercise.</p><h2>Child voice is optional</h2><p>Begin off-screen and parent-led. A reported quote is not direct testimony. Declining is not low trust. Never make the child responsible for regulating or grading a parent; no child-owned device or direct chatbot is needed.</p><h2>Parent privacy is a separate boundary</h2><p>Parent stress, guilt, trauma and mental-health notes must not silently enter a child-facing model, co-parent account or external assistant. Current code’s whole-profile synthesis coupling must be addressed before reuse.</p><p class="small">No automatic detection, safeguarding guarantee or downstream deletion promise. Rights, provider child-data/ZDR eligibility, SIWC commercial access, policy/legal review and secure lifecycle remain unresolved real-data gates.</p>''')
page('What we tested.<br><em>What would change our mind.</em>','''<div class="two"><article><h2>Passed locally</h2><p>16 model tests; 14 browser checks; five desktop/mobile screenshots. Correction clears stale context/plan and blocks edited free-text export. Safety hold blocks ordinary actions/sharing.</p></article><article><h2>Not established</h2><p>Adaptive coaching, clinical safety, efficacy, actual family demand, hands-on competitors, licensing or provider approval. Production backend/web/iOS checks unrun; no product code changed.</p></article></div><h2>The next comparison</h2><p>Matched histories/time: short reviewed summary, competent generic assistant, guided practice card, and authorized Mango/GiGi/Hatley use. Judge controllable parent action, supported interpretation, correction fidelity, capacity fit and burden. Warmth and logs are not relational outcomes.</p><p>Before real-family research: expert/rights/privacy/provider gates, age-appropriate licensed measures and independent observation. A parent self-report cannot stand in for child experience. Sample size follows the intended claim and precision, not an arbitrary “validation N.”</p><p>Stop or simplify if profiling ties simpler reflection, guilt/pressure increases, effects depend on omitted human support, or measured gains are only compliance. No score ships on the strength of analogy.</p><h2>Read, copy and inspect</h2><ul><li><a href="strategy.md">Full current strategy</a> and <a href="examples.md">synthetic before/after examples</a>.</li><li><a href="research-prompt-addendum.md">Reusable iteration-2 research prompt addendum</a> plus preserved <a href="../research/parent_profile_deep_research_prompt.md">original prompt</a>.</li><li><a href="research/parent_iteration2_alliance_evidence.md">Science/measures</a>, <a href="research/parent_iteration2_good_inside.md">Good Inside</a>, <a href="research/parent_iteration2_competitors.md">competitors</a>.</li><li><a href="verification.md">Passed versus unrun checks</a>; <a href="README.md">artifact index and worker reports</a>.</li></ul><p class="small">Sources preserved as authored; external links retained, not re-browsed by local renderer. Vendor claims, primary evidence, design inference and executed tests remain distinct.</p>''')
css='''@page{size:A4;margin:0}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#ddd;color:#263c36;font:12pt/1.45 Arial,sans-serif}.sheet{position:relative;width:210mm;height:297mm;padding:17mm 18mm 20mm;background:#fbfaf6;margin:8mm auto;break-after:page;overflow:hidden}.eyebrow{font-size:8pt;color:#245e54;letter-spacing:1.3px;margin-bottom:7mm}h1{font:34pt/1.08 Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 7mm}h1 em{color:#245e54}h2{font:19pt Georgia,serif;margin:6mm 0 3mm}p{margin:3mm 0}.lead{font-size:17pt}.small,figcaption{font-size:8.4pt;color:#586860;line-height:1.4}.callout{padding:5mm;background:#e8eee3;border-left:3px solid #245e54;margin:6mm 0}.two{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:5mm}article{padding:4mm;background:#eee9df;border-radius:3mm}article p{font-size:10.5pt}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:10pt;margin:4mm 0}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:3mm;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5c9}th{background:#e8eee3}td:first-child{font-weight:bold}figure{margin:4mm 0}img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:contain;border:1px solid #d4d9cf}.screen img{max-height:90mm}.hero img{max-height:155mm}.diagram img{max-height:55mm}a{color:#245e54}ul{font-size:10pt;padding-left:5mm}li{margin:2mm 0}footer{position:absolute;bottom:10mm;left:18mm;right:18mm;border-top:1px solid #d4d9cf;padding-top:3mm;font-size:8pt;color:#586860}footer span{float:right}@media print{body{background:white}.sheet{margin:0}}'''
(root/'strategy-print.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Next Level iteration 2: practice how you show up</title><style>'+css+'</style></head><body>'+''.join(pages)+'</body></html>')
print(f'Built {len(pages)} pages')
